158.stem:
Eli is choosing between two investment options.

\begin{framed}Option 1: Depositing a single amount of $\text{\textdollar}40\,000$ today, earning interest of $1.2\%$ per annum, compounded monthly.\end{framed}

\begin{framed}Option 2: Depositing $\text{\textdollar}1000$ at the end of each quarter, earning interest of $2.4\%$ per annum, compounded quarterly.\end{framed}

A table of future value interest factors for an annuity of $\text{\textdollar}1$ is shown.

\extable{Tq158_1}

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{1356_q30_s1}

Jonathan wins on the third spin if the first two spins are green (spin again) and the third is blue:
$$\begin{aligned}P(\text{Jonathan wins})&=\dfrac{1}{2}\times\dfrac{1}{2}\times\dfrac{3}{10}\\&=\dfrac{3}{40}\end{aligned}$$

