solutions.latex:
\exfigure{309_q35_s1}

Charlie wins on her first toss ($\bar{M}C$) or her second toss ($\bar{M}\bar{C}\bar{M}C$):
$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{Charlie wins 1st or 2nd}) &= P(\bar{M}C)+P(\bar{M}\bar{C}\bar{M}C) \\ &= \dfrac{1}{2}\times\dfrac{1}{3}+\dfrac{1}{2}\times\dfrac{2}{3}\times\dfrac{1}{2}\times\dfrac{1}{3} \\ &= \dfrac{2}{9} \end{aligned}$$
